        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 78-year-old female patient, admitted on 10/07/2011 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management. Her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged in stable condition on 11/07/2011. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. I recommend continuation of her regular COPD medication and pulmonary rehabilitation referral.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
